  "problem": "What is the value of $\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
  "worked_solution": "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-8+3) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+81÷3}-(-5) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{1+27}+5 & = \\\\ \\sqrt{28}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{28}≈5‭.291\\,503\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{28}+5 & ≈ \\\\ ‭‭‭5.291\\,503+5 & = \\\\ 10.291\\,503 & ≈ \\\\ 10.292\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
